{
  "collections": [
    {
      "description": "Chess rule-conformance battery for the eval-chess-frontend pure-frontend chess web app (Vite + TS + chess.js, exposed DOM contract). Each rule is a sequence of pagehub-browser calls (type fen-input, click apply-fen, type uci-input, click submit-move, get-attribute data-fen / data-status off [data-testid=\"board\"]). Covers: legal move accepted (data-fen changes); illegal-given-position rejected (data-fen UNCHANGED); kingside castling; queenside castling; castling rights respected (no-K-right -> e1g1 rejected); en passant capture; promotion to queen; pinned piece cannot move; checkmate -> data-status=\"white_won\"; stalemate -> data-status=\"draw\"; 50-move rule (halfmove 99 -> non-pawn non-capture -> data-status=\"draw\"). All FENs python-chess-derived; terminal assertions are claim-aware. Dropped (tight on the 50-item collection cap; documented here so future readers know what is NOT covered): threefold repetition (8 setup moves = ~20 requests, blew the cap); underpromotion to N/R/B (engine-identical to queen for the rule-conformance check); castle-through-check and move-into-check as separate scenarios (same underlying rule as pin: a move that leaves the own king in check is rejected, exercised by S5).",
      "items": [
        "lifecycle-01-create-session",
        "lifecycle-02-navigate",
        "s1-castle-k-type-fen",
        "s1-castle-k-apply",
        "s1-castle-k-type-uci-e1g1",
        "s1-castle-k-submit-e1g1",
